      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/persistence/export-snapshot.ts",
      "content": "This check precedes reading the stored schema, so a genuine older database with a newer supplied layout returns `ReadFailed` for an absent store rather than the documented `UnknownLayout`. For example, schema 1 with layout 7 lacks `observations`. Read `meta` and available layout stores in the same transaction, check the schema mismatch first, and only then report missing stores for an otherwise matching layout.",
      "existing_code": "    const missing = ['meta', ...layout.stores].find((store) =\u003e !db.objectStoreNames.contains(store));\n    if (missing) return { kind: 'ReadFailed', store: missing as WorkspaceStore };",
      "start_line": 61,
      "end_line": 62,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/persistence/export-snapshot.ts",
      "content": "If an accidentally async `onBatch` throws or returns a rejected promise, this branch aborts the transaction and returns `EarlyAutoCommitGuard`, but leaves the returned promise's rejection unhandled. The caller cannot catch that rejection through `readExportSnapshot`, since this method resolves with the guard result. Consume the rejected thenable when detecting it (while still aborting immediately), and add a rejected-promise test alongside the resolved-promise case.",
      "existing_code": "            if (typeof (returned as { then?: unknown } | undefined)?.then === 'function') {\n              fail({ kind: 'EarlyAutoCommitGuard' });",
